To center the image horizontally, you can add the class "block" to the image tag and use Flexbox to center the image. Here's an updated version of your code that centers the image horizontally:

```
import React from 'react';

const Home = () => {
  return (
    <>
      <div className="flex justify-center">
        <img className="block mx-auto" src="https://picsum.photos/400" alt="My Photo" />
      </div>
      <h1 className="text-center">Welcome to My Personal Website</h1>
    </>
  );
};

export default Home;
```

In the modified code, I added the `flex` and `justify-center` classes to the wrapping div element to create a flex container and align its children (image) in the center horizontally. The `block mx-auto` classes added to the image element center the image within the container.
